# REQ-008: Annotations & Highlights

**Priority:** Must Have
**Effort:** Medium
**Risk:** High (system annotation boundary means EMIS Web annotations are not visible in EMIS-X; user must be clearly notified)
**Depends On:** REQ-004 (Document Viewer & Navigation), REQ-005 (File Format Support & Conversion)

---

## User Story

As a practice administrator or clinician,
I need to add highlights, comments, and drawings to documents in EMIS-X, and be clearly informed about which system annotations were created in and where they are visible,
So that I can communicate context and instructions to colleagues without missing clinical notes that exist only in EMIS Web, and without exposing patient-sensitive annotations inappropriately.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Users can highlight text within a document in EMIS-X. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Users can add free-text comments/notes to a document in EMIS-X. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Users can add drawings/markup to a document in EMIS-X. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Annotations created in EMIS-X are visible to all users within the same practice when using EMIS-X. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Annotations created in EMIS-X are **not** visible in EMIS Web (Phase 2 deferred — see constraint below). *(Must Have — explicit boundary)*
- [ ] Annotations created in EMIS Web are visible in EMIS Web as normal; they are **not** visible in EMIS-X (Phase 2 deferred — see constraint below). *(Must Have — explicit boundary)*
- [ ] When a document is opened in EMIS-X and EMIS Web annotations exist for that document, the EMIS-X viewer displays a clear, persistent notice informing the user that this document has annotations in EMIS Web that are not visible in EMIS-X, and directing them to EMIS Web to view those annotations. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Every annotation displays a system-origin indicator showing which system it was created in ("EMIS-X" or "EMIS Web") and which system(s) it is visible in. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Each annotation has a per-annotation toggle controlling whether the patient can see it when viewing their record via online access (e.g. NHS App / Patient Access). *(Must Have)*
- [ ] All filed documents are audited. *(Must Have)*

