## System Annotation Boundary (Architectural Constraint)

> **Documents Management Core operates with a clean system annotation boundary: each system displays only the annotations created within it.**
>
> - **EMIS-X annotations:** Created and visible in EMIS-X only. Not visible in EMIS Web in Core.
> - **EMIS Web annotations:** Created and visible in EMIS Web only (via Atalasoft). Not visible in EMIS-X in Core.
>
> **Why:** EMIS Web uses an Atalasoft component to store and render document annotations. This component is not accessible from EMIS-X. Rather than generating burnt-in copies (which adds architectural complexity and risk to Core delivery), the boundary is made explicit to the user in both systems.
>
> **Clinical safety implication:** A user viewing a document in EMIS-X will not see any annotations added in EMIS Web. This is a real clinical risk (HAZ-DOC-021). The mitigation is a mandatory, persistent system notice in the EMIS-X viewer whenever EMIS Web annotations exist for that document, directing the user to EMIS Web to review them.
>
> **Phase 2 deferred:** Cross-system annotation visibility (EMIS-X annotations visible in EMIS Web and vice versa) is deferred beyond the 30-day Core delivery window. V1b to define the architecture for cross-system annotation sync. V1e to assess clinical safety implications before cross-system visibility is enabled.

