## Patient Visibility Toggle — IG Note

> ⚠️ **Clinically and IG-sensitive control.**
> The per-annotation patient visibility toggle directly controls what a patient sees when accessing their record online. This must default to **not visible to patient** (privacy-preserving default per IG-002) and require an explicit action to make an annotation patient-visible. The toggle state must be auditable.

---

## Dimension 1: Clinical Safety

### Applicable Guardrails
- **CLIN-002:** Patient Data Audit Trail — annotation creation, amendment, deletion, and patient visibility toggle changes must all be audited
- **CLIN-005:** Clinical Decision Support Transparency — annotations used to convey clinical context/instructions must be clearly attributed to their author and timestamp
- **CLIN-007:** Hazard Mitigation Evidence — when a document has EMIS Web annotations, the EMIS-X viewer must display a persistent, unmissable notice; the user must not open a document in EMIS-X and be unaware that annotations exist in EMIS Web

### Hazards Addressed

- **HAZ-DOC-021:** Clinician reads a document in EMIS-X without seeing EMIS Web annotations — clinical context or instructions from EMIS Web missed; incorrect clinical action taken
  - **Severity:** Critical
  - **Likelihood:** Medium (affects all documents that have been annotated in EMIS Web or DocMan)
  - **Risk Level:** Critical — mitigated by mandatory persistent EMIS-X system boundary notice; residual risk remains until cross-system annotation visibility is delivered in Phase 2

- **HAZ-DOC-023:** Patient-sensitive annotation (e.g. clinician note not intended for patient) inadvertently visible to patient via online record access
  - **Severity:** High
  - **Likelihood:** Medium (if toggle defaults to visible)
  - **Risk Level:** High

- **HAZ-DOC-024:** Annotation attribution lost or incorrect — clinician cannot determine who added a note or when
  - **Severity:** Medium
  - **Likelihood:** Low
  - **Risk Level:** Medium

### Mitigations

- **MIT-DOC-020:** When a document has EMIS Web annotations, EMIS-X displays a persistent, unmissable system boundary notice in the document viewer; notice includes a prompt directing the user to EMIS Web to view those annotations
  - **Type:** UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Partial (informs user; does not show the annotation content — residual risk until Phase 2 cross-system sync)

- **MIT-DOC-020a:** Every annotation displays a system-origin indicator ("Created in EMIS-X — visible in EMIS-X only" / "Created in EMIS Web — visible in EMIS Web only") so users are never ambiguous about annotation scope
  - **Type:** UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete (for transparency)
- **MIT-DOC-021:** Patient visibility toggle defaults to **not visible to patient**; explicit action required to make annotation patient-visible
  - **Type:** Business Logic + UI Control
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

- **MIT-DOC-022:** Every annotation stores author ERN and creation timestamp; displayed to all practice users viewing the annotation
  - **Type:** Business Logic
  - **Effectiveness:** Complete

