## Dimension 2: Information Governance

### Applicable Guardrails
- **IG-002:** Privacy by Design and Default — patient visibility toggle defaults to not visible; opt-in to patient visibility, not opt-out
- **IG-003:** Lawful Basis Declaration — Article 6(1)(e) public task + Article 9(2)(h) health data; patient visibility decision is a clinical/administrative judgement
- **IG-004:** Special Category Data Protection — annotations are special category data; stored encrypted at rest (AES-256-GCM)
- **IG-005:** Data Subject Rights — patient has right of access to annotations marked as patient-visible; annotations marked not-visible are withheld under appropriate exemption (clinical privilege / third-party information)
- **IG-008:** Consent Management — patient visibility toggle state must be auditable; changes logged with user ERN and timestamp

### Data Handling
- Annotation content stored server-side, encrypted at rest, scoped to practice
- Patient visibility toggle state stored as a boolean flag per annotation with full change history
- Burnt-in copy stored as a separate document rendition; original preserved and never modified
- Annotation author ERN stored; never plain username or NHS number

### GDPR Articles
- **Article 5(1)(f):** Integrity and confidentiality — annotations treated as special category health data
- **Article 9(2)(h):** Special category — medical purposes
- **Article 15:** Right of access — patient-visible annotations accessible to patient on subject access request
- **Article 17:** Right to erasure — annotation deletion must be auditable; consider retention obligations before erasure

---

## Dimension 3: Security

### Applicable Guardrails
- **AUTH-004:** Authorization Required — annotation endpoints require valid JWT; patient visibility toggle changes require appropriate role scope
- **SEC-001:** TLS Encryption — annotation content transmitted over TLS 1.2+

### Security Requirements
- Free-text comment content sanitised to prevent XSS when rendered in the viewer
- Drawing/markup data validated server-side; malformed annotation payloads rejected
- Patient visibility toggle state changes restricted to users with appropriate role (e.g. clinician or senior admin); configurable per practice

---

## Dimension 4: Observability & Performance

### KPIs
- Annotation creation rate by type (highlight / comment / drawing)
- Patient visibility toggle usage rate (proportion of annotations marked patient-visible)
- System boundary notice display rate (proportion of document opens where the EMIS Web annotation notice is shown)
- Annotation load time (document opened with annotations → annotations rendered)

### OTEL Spans
- `documents.annotation.created` — new annotation created; type, author ERN, and origin system recorded
- `documents.annotation.amended` — existing annotation edited
- `documents.annotation.deleted` — annotation deleted
- `documents.annotation.patient_visibility_changed` — patient visibility toggle state changed; new state recorded
- `documents.annotation.emis_web_notice_shown` — EMIS-X system boundary notice displayed because EMIS Web annotations exist for this document

### SLOs
- Annotation render (document with annotations): p95 < 2 seconds
- Annotation save (create/amend): p95 < 1 second
- System boundary notice render: p95 < 500ms from document open to notice displayed

