## ✨ Evaluation Function Specification

### CHECK 1: CLIN-007 — EMIS Web Annotation Boundary Notice is Persistent and Unmissable
- **Trigger:** User opens a document in EMIS-X that has annotations in EMIS Web
- **Test Scenario:** System boundary notice
  - Validation 1: A clear notice is displayed in the EMIS-X viewer informing the user that EMIS Web annotations exist for this document and are not visible in EMIS-X
  - Validation 2: The notice includes a prompt or link directing the user to open the document in EMIS Web to view those annotations
  - Validation 3: The notice is visible without any additional user action (not hidden in a menu or collapsed by default)
  - Validation 4: The notice cannot be permanently dismissed in a way that prevents it appearing on future opens of the same document
- **Guardrail:** CLIN-007
- **Hazard:** HAZ-DOC-021
- **Pass Criteria:** Notice always displayed when EMIS Web annotations exist; persistent; includes EMIS Web redirect prompt

### CHECK 2: CLIN-007 — System-Origin Indicator on Every Annotation
- **Trigger:** Document opened with one or more EMIS-X annotations
- **Test Scenario:** System-origin indicator visibility
  - Validation 1: Each annotation clearly indicates it was created in EMIS-X and is visible in EMIS-X only
  - Validation 2: No annotation appears without a system-origin label
  - Validation 3: System-origin label is not removable or hideable by the viewing user
- **Guardrail:** CLIN-007
- **Hazard:** HAZ-DOC-021
- **Pass Criteria:** Every annotation has a system-origin indicator; always visible

### CHECK 3: IG-002 — Patient Visibility Toggle Defaults to Not Visible
- **Trigger:** New annotation created
- **Test Scenario:** Default toggle state
  - Validation 1: Newly created annotation has patient visibility = false by default
  - Validation 2: No annotation is patient-visible without an explicit user action to enable it
  - Validation 3: Default cannot be changed via a user-supplied parameter in the creation request (server enforces default)
- **Guardrail:** IG-002
- **Hazard:** HAZ-DOC-023
- **Pass Criteria:** Patient visibility always defaults to false; server-enforced

### CHECK 4: CLIN-002 — Annotation Actions Audited
- **Trigger:** Any annotation action (create, amend, delete, toggle patient visibility)
- **Test Scenario:** Audit log completeness
  - Validation 1: Audit entry created for each action containing: `action`, `user_ern`, `document_ern`, `annotation_id`, `timestamp` (ISO 8601)
  - Validation 2: Patient visibility toggle change audit entry records both previous and new state
  - Validation 3: Audit entries do not contain annotation free-text content (content stored separately)
- **Guardrail:** CLIN-002
- **Hazard:** HAZ-DOC-023, HAZ-DOC-024
- **Pass Criteria:** All annotation actions audited; toggle state changes include before/after values

### CHECK 5: CLIN-005 — Annotation Attribution Always Displayed
- **Trigger:** Document opened with one or more annotations
- **Test Scenario:** Author and timestamp visibility
  - Validation 1: Each annotation displays the author's name (derived from ERN) and creation timestamp
  - Validation 2: Attribution cannot be hidden or removed by the viewing user
  - Validation 3: Author ERN stored server-side; display name resolved at render time (not stored as plain text)
- **Guardrail:** CLIN-005
- **Hazard:** HAZ-DOC-024
- **Pass Criteria:** Every annotation attributed to author + timestamp; attribution always visible

### CHECK 6: SEC — Free-text Comment XSS Prevention
- **Trigger:** Free-text annotation content rendered in viewer
- **Test Scenario:** XSS injection in comment
  - Input: Annotation comment containing `<script>alert('xss')</script>`
  - Validation 1: Script tag not executed in viewer
  - Validation 2: Content rendered as escaped plain text
  - Validation 3: No browser alert or DOM manipulation triggered
- **Guardrail:** SEC-001
- **Pass Criteria:** Free-text annotation content always HTML-escaped on render; XSS not possible

