## PxD (Added by V1d)

> **Scope: Full PxD.** UI surfaces: annotation panel (side panel inside viewer), EMIS Web boundary notice (persistent, undismissable), annotation type toolbar (highlight / comment / drawing), add-annotation form, annotation list with author attribution, patient visibility toggle, annotation delete confirmation.

---

### User Flow

**Primary Flow — Add a comment annotation:**
1. Clinician opens a document in the viewer; annotation panel is visible in the right pane (Protocol Panel)
2. Clinician clicks "✏️ Annotations" button in the viewer toolbar — annotation panel scrolls to annotation section (or panel opens if collapsed)
3. EMIS Web boundary notice is shown at top of panel if EMIS Web annotations exist for this document — this notice cannot be dismissed
4. Clinician clicks "Comment" tool button — add-annotation form expands below the toolbar
5. Clinician types comment text in `Textarea`; patient visibility defaults to "Not visible to patient"
6. Clinician clicks "Save annotation" — annotation saved; appears in annotation list with author name, role, timestamp, and system-origin badge ("EMIS-X")
7. `Notification variant="success"` shown: `{t('annotations.saved.success')}`

**Primary Flow — Add a highlight:**
1. Clinician selects text in the document viewer by clicking and dragging
2. A "Highlight" contextual button appears near the selection (or clinician clicks "Highlight" in annotation toolbar)
3. Highlight applied; optionally clinician adds a note in the form that appears
4. Highlight saved; appears in annotation list with page/position reference

**Error Flow — Viewer unavailable:**
- Annotation panel shown but form disabled; `Banner variant="warning"` + `{t('annotations.viewerUnavailable')}`

**Exit Types:**
- Save: annotation saved; form collapses; list updates
- Cancel: form collapses; no annotation created
- Navigate away: annotation list persists; panel state restored on return

