### Accessibility Requirements (WCAG 2.1 AAA — clinical data)

> AAA required: annotations are clinical metadata; patient visibility setting has direct clinical safety impact (HAZ-DOC-023).

- [x] Perceivable: EMIS Web boundary notice uses `Banner variant="warning"` (colour + icon + text); system-origin badge uses `Badge` with text label (not colour alone)
- [x] Operable: all annotation tools keyboard-accessible; `Tab` navigates toolbar; `Space/Enter` activates; annotation list navigable by keyboard
- [x] Understandable: patient visibility defaults to "Not visible to patient" with label confirming this is the IG-safe default; EMIS Web boundary notice includes source reference (CLIN-007 · HAZ-DOC-021 · MIT-DOC-020) so clinician understands why it appears
- [x] Robust: `jest-axe ^9.0.0`; all interactive elements are `@emisgroup/ui-*`; live region on annotation list

**Rule A — all inputs labelled:**
```tsx
<Textarea aria-label={t('annotations.comment.label')} ... />
<Select aria-label={t('annotations.patientVisibility.label')} ... />
```

**Rule B — live regions:**
```tsx
<div role="status" aria-live="polite">{isLoading && t('annotations.saving')}</div>
<div role="alert" aria-live="assertive">{error && t('annotations.error.save')}</div>
<ul role="list" aria-label={t('annotations.list.label')} aria-live="polite">
  {annotations.map(a => <li key={a.id}><AnnotationItem annotation={a} /></li>)}
</ul>
```

